Q: Render Hider hierarchy based on IFC spatial / assembly structure instead of IFC entity type A: <p>Your implementation can be split into two steps.</p>
<ol>
<li>First, query the model spatial structure using the <a href="https://github.com/ThatOpen/engine_fragment/blob/391f9dc1e1ccf2e9b12987ffb430ae0b144cd551/packages/fragments/src/FragmentsModels/src/model/fragments-model.ts#L218" rel="nofollow noreferrer">getSpatialStructure command</a>. You can use that hierarchical object model to build your UI tree.</li>
</ol>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/JlDGIS2C.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/JlDGIS2C.png" alt="Spatial Structure" /></a></p>
<ol start="2">
<li>Then, If the entity &quot;IFCELEMENTASSEMBLY&quot; exists in the model you can attach a click event handler to the corresponding tree item that takes the Assembly's localID (provided by the spatial structure object), collects the IDs of its decomposed elements, and passes those IDs to the hider using the modelIdMap parameter.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>  const assemblyRelations = await model.getRelations([AssemblyID]);
  const children = assemblyRelations.get(AssemblyID)?.data[&quot;IsDecomposedBy&quot;];

  const modelIdMap: OBC.ModelIdMap = {};
  const hider = components.get(OBC.Hider);
  modelIdMap[model.modelId] = new Set(children);
  await hider.set(false, modelIdMap);
</code></pre>
<p>Let me know if you need any other clarifications!</p>

Q: How to decrypt PKCS#7 encrypted data in C#? A: <p>I found <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20100327135133/http://www.example-code.com/csharp/crypt_decrypt_p7m.asp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">an example</a> of how to decrypt PKCS#7 in C#. It may be enough to get you started.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>Chilkat.Crypt2 crypt = new Chilkat.Crypt2();

//  Any string argument automatically begins the 30-day trial.
bool success;
success = crypt.UnlockComponent(&quot;30-day trial&quot;);
if (success != true) {
    MessageBox.Show(&quot;Crypt component unlock failed&quot;);
    return;
}

crypt.CryptAlgorithm = &quot;pki&quot;;

//  To decrypt in memory:
//  
byte[] p7mData = crypt.ReadFile(&quot;test.p7m&quot;);

byte [] decrypted = crypt.DecryptBytes(p7mData);

string decryptedStr = System.Text.Encoding.ASCII.GetString(decrypted);

textBox1.Text = decryptedStr;

//  To decrypt you'll need the private key.
//  Also, the certificate should have already been installed
//  on the computer.  This is typically achieved by installing
//  from a .pfx file, or by importing from a certificate
//  authority's online web application.  If you are decrypting
//  from ASP, ASP.NET, or a Windows Service, you'll need to
//  import in a way that provides the calling process permission
//  to access and use the private key.  The procedure for
//  doing this is explained here:
//  http://blog.chilkatsoft.com/?p=149
//  Also, there is no &quot;SetDecryptCert&quot; method.  The .p7m
//  contains information that allows the Chilkat component
//  to locate the certificate to be used for decryption.
//  The Chilkat Crypt component automatically searches
//  the Windows Current User certificate store and the
//  Local Machine certificate store.

//  For file-to-file decryption:
success = crypt.CkDecryptFile(&quot;dude.p7m&quot;,&quot;dudeOut.gif&quot;);
if (success != true) {
    MessageBox.Show(crypt.LastErrorText);
    return;
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to use API 3x-ui? A: <p>You can use 3x-ui php sdk :
<a href="https://github.com/es-taheri/3x-ui" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/es-taheri/3x-ui</a>
Example:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>use XUI\Xray\Inbound\Protocols\Vmess\Vmess;
use XUI\Xui;

require_once __DIR__.'/vendor/autoload.php';
$xui = new Xui($xui_host, $xui_port, $xui_path, $xui_ssl);
$result = $xui-&gt;login($username, $password);
@$response = $result-&gt;repsonse;
if ($result-&gt;ok &amp;&amp; $response-&gt;success) {
    $xui_inbound = $xui-&gt;xray-&gt;inbound;
    $config = new Vmess();
    $config-&gt;settings-&gt;add_client();
    $config-&gt;stream_settings-&gt;ws_settings(false, '/3x-ui');
    $result = $xui_inbound-&gt;add($config, 'Test 3x-ui', 100 * Xui::UNIT_GIGABYTE, 86400);
    @$response = $result-&gt;repsonse;
    if ($result-&gt;ok &amp;&amp; $response-&gt;success) {
        $inbound_id = $response-&gt;obj-&gt;id;
        var_dump(&quot;Inbound added : #$inbound_id&quot;);
    } else {
        $error = $result-&gt;error ?? $response-&gt;msg;
        var_dump(&quot;Add inbound failed! (Error: $error)&quot;);
    }
} else {
    $error = $result-&gt;error ?? $response-&gt;msg;
    var_dump(&quot;Login failed! (Error: $error)&quot;);
}
</code></pre>

Q: Change Color of Entry Underline or Remove this Color A: <ol>
<li><p>In .NET MAUI, each cross‑platform control (like <code>Entry</code>/<code>Editor</code>) is rendered by a <strong>handler</strong> on each platform.</p>
</li>
<li><p><code>EntryHandler</code> and <code>EditorHandler</code> let you <strong>map extra configuration</strong> to the native Android views when those controls are created.</p>
</li>
<li><p><code>AppendToMapping(&quot;NoUnderline&quot;, …)</code> adds a mapping block (tagged with the key <code>&quot;NoUnderline&quot;</code>) that runs for <strong>Android only</strong> (due to <code>#if ANDROID</code>) to adjust the <strong>native view</strong> (an Android <code>EditText</code>).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>In MauiProgram.cs</p>
<pre><code>        // Remove the native underline/background on Entry for Android
        EntryHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping(&quot;NoUnderline&quot;, (handler, view) =&gt;
        {

#if ANDROID
            var e = handler.PlatformView;

            // Remove default underline/background &amp; minimum height
            e.Background = null;
            e.SetMinHeight(0);
            e.SetMinimumHeight(0);

            // Center text vertically inside the native control
            e.Gravity = GravityFlags.CenterVertical;
#endif
        });
        // Remove the native underline/background on Editor for Android
        EditorHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping(&quot;NoUnderline&quot;, (handler, view) =&gt;
        {
#if ANDROID
            var e = handler.PlatformView;

            // Remove default underline/background &amp; minimum height
            e.Background = null;
            e.SetMinHeight(0);
            e.SetMinimumHeight(0);

#endif
        });
</code></pre>
